# JOBS lives here, not in the jobspec. mesosci/DEFAULTS.env sets JOBS=24 as a
# plain assignment and source_env_files runs AFTER the job environment, so
# whatever ci-linux-arm.nomad exports is silently overridden. This file is the
# only place a per-container value takes effect.
#
# 30 = the cores ci-linux-arm reserves per worker. That is the rule slc10's
# DEFAULTS.env argues for at length, and the rule it learned the hard way: the
# 2026-08-31 roll doubled the x86 allocation but left JOBS at 14, so three
# builders compiling 14-wide on 24 cores were slower than the six 14-wide-on-12
# they replaced. Resizing the allocation without moving JOBS is only half the
# change.
#
# Memory is not the binding constraint here, unlike on slc10. alieevee-wn-8 has
# 1004 GiB and each worker reserves 180000 MiB, so 30 compiles get ~6 GiB each
# against slc10's ~4.3 -- comfortable even for the 7-10 GiB O2Physics
# translation units. If OOM kills do appear, lower this rather than raising the
# reservation: three workers share one node with bb-services and
# jenkins-builder, and taking more memory here takes it from them.
#
# Not oversubscribed: the task is bounded by a reserved cpuset of 30, so asking
# for more than the entitlement buys throttling and context switches rather than
# parallelism.
JOBS=30
